projectdescription:
Certified Professional Program - New Building - To construct a 6 storey with 69 Supportive Housing from 2nd to 6th floors with retails and residential ancillary uses on the main floor with no parking. Basement and main level are of concrete construction. Levels 2-6 are of wood frame construction. 
(No kitchen Exhaust ducts proposed. Only HVAC ducts at the main ceiling level.)

VBBL 2019 - Reviewed during 2020/2021 Pandemic.

STAGE 1 - Excavation and Shoring issued on April 14, 2021. 
STGAE 2 - Full Construction issued on June 25, 2021.
Rev# 1 (Apr. 21, 2022) - Interior and exterior changes on the following:

- changing from Affordable Housing to Supportive Housing;
- expanding the North retail unit;
- eliminating the South retail unit;
- expanding Amenity spaces with servery function, calming room and 
  security office at the first floor;
- reducing Class B bike stalls from 12 stalls to 8 stalls; and,
- adding a heat treatment room.

Rev# 2 - (Apr. 28, 2023) - Interior and exterior alterations and change of major occupancy per the following below and change of owners from Anhart Community to the City of Vancouver. 

- a change of use from Retail to Social Service Centre;
- changing Unit #210 from a 2 bedroom dwelling to ancillary office space
- updated interior details;
- removal of the Tensarch structure from the roof and addition of an 
  overhang, and;
- corrected Landscape drawing for Level 1 to show the correct mosaic tile 
  in the residential entry alcove.

Field Review - Addition / Alteration - Interior alterations to provide improvements to the generator in the parkade level of this multiple dwelling building on this site.  Work to replace the emergency generator and automatic transfer switch.

OK for Field Review per W.Wong, February 23, 2021

Letters of assurance submitted by: Schedule A and Schedule B: Victor Lu - 778-927-3429;

High Density Housing / Commercial - Addition / Alteration - Exterior and interior alterations to install a heat pump unit on the roof to provide heating and cooling to this existing Heritage Class B Institutional (Police Station) building. Scope of works include:
- add new supplemental electric heating boilers;
- new pumps and mechanical equipment to suit new plant level upgrades;
- new electrical and structural supports to suit new mechanical equipment;
- re-roofing details to show roof mounted supports for new rooftop unit; and
- DDC control upgrades to operate new mechanical equipment. 

******THIS PERMIT HAS BEEN ISSUED UNDER THE REQUIREMENTS OF VBBL 2019 AND REVIEWED DURING THE 2020 COVID-19 PANDEMIC CRISIS. ********

Building Review Branch Notes:
1. Ok for DB per Shelley Durgaro on March 18, 2020.
2. Sch-A, Mech. B, Arch. B, Struct. B & Elec. B are submitted.

Low Density Housing - Addition / Alteration - HRC - Exterior and interior alteration to this existing SFD. Scope of work to include:
- new exterior cladding to replace all existing cladding;
- interior layout changes to both main and upper level;
- replace some windows and doors; and,
- repairs to existing roof as needed. 

Revision #1: Gas fireplace previously proposed is cancelled. Infill existing door from foyer to living room and make a new opening from living to kitchen. New exterior rear door in kitchen. New guest bath and master W.I.C. No Project Value added. Sch C-B (Jason Hui, 778-319-3409) & C-D provided (Sunil Bhanot, 604-575-8220) provided.

Low Density Housing - Addition / Alteration - CF-2021-009796

interior changes to this existing one family dwelling.

Scope of work:

- convert the attached garage to Rec. Room;
- new layout on Main floor;
- added one bathroom;
- removed one window in the exiting rec room and install two new windows in the new washroom and new rec room.

Structural Schedule B provided by Antony Wang. P. Eng. 604.618.6236

REUP submitted by Sukhi Thind, BC Energy House Inc - no upgrades required
